Well, the standard approach is to linearly scan through with a running minimum, initializing with the first element and comparing each subsequent one. But let me push back a bit—this obsession with *finding* the minimum often papers over deeper design questions. Why isn't your data structured to make this trivial from the start? A min-heap, a sorted container, even a simple running tracker updated on insertion—all of these avoid the very need for this algorithm.

Still, if you're saddled with an unsorted array and truly must solve what is fundamentally a problem of your own prior structuring, here's the straightforward method:

